# Conventional Commits

When creating git commits (and when pushing to GitHub), write commit messages in **English** following [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

## Types

- `feat`: new feature
- `fix`: bug fix
- `docs`: documentation only
- `style`: formatting (no code change)
- `refactor`: neither fix nor feature
- `perf`: performance improvement
- `test`: adding or fixing tests
- `build`: build system or dependencies
- `ci`: CI configuration
- `chore`: maintenance tasks

## Rules

- Description in English, imperative mood, concise
- Do not capitalize the first letter of the description
- No period at the end of the subject line
- Use `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer or `!` after type/scope when applicable

## Examples

```
chore: add gitignore for Xcode and Cursor
feat(paywall): show trial period on subscribe screen
fix(storekit): handle failed purchase restoration
```